  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing Prosecutions of Traffickers and Improving Protections of Vulnerable Workers in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Solidarity Center (SC) project aims to improve the record of prosecutions and civil cases in key transit and destination areas of Indonesia. This project will improve the enforcement of existing laws and empower civil society actors to advocate for greater implementation of established TIP policies at the local level. In improving and expanding legal and other direct protection services SC will deploy a legal consultant and build a larger cadre of legal advocates to represent trafficking victims. SC will partner with the International Catholic Migration Commission to train and build capacity for service providers and lawyers. The project will also result in a report on best practices learned through these activities.</narrative>
  </description>
